# ============================================================================
# Phase 7 Scenario 2 — Post-overdose MOUD linkage
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Intent: agents who survive a nonfatal overdose are linked to MOUD at the
# encounter, rather than at the baseline's elevated-but-partial rate.
#
# CORRECTED 2026-08-17. The previous version asked whether an engine change was
# needed in moud.py STEP 4. It is not — see MECHANISM below.
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MECHANISM (read this before choosing a value)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# titan/features/moud.py computes the per-step initiation probability as:
#
#     p_start  = moud.reinit_prob            # top-level calibration override
#     p_start *= moud.post_relapse_rr        # if recent relapse
#     p_start *= moud.post_overdose_rr       # if recent_overdose is set
#     p_start  = min(1.0, max(0.0, p_start)) # clamped
#
# So post_overdose_rr is a MULTIPLIER on an already-fitted probability, and the
# linkage rate it produces is p_start x rr, not rr. The window it applies over is
# overdose.post_overdose_window (titan/params/overdose.yml), which owns the
# `recent_overdose` flag — there is no separate moud window.
#
# CONSEQUENCE: the value depends on the refit's fitted reinit_prob and cannot be
# written down until the refit lands. Use the formulas below.
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EVIDENCE
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# D'Onofrio et al., JAMA 2015;313(16):1636-1644 — RCT of ED-initiated
# buprenorphine/naloxone. Engagement in formal addiction treatment at 30 days:
#
#     ED-initiated buprenorphine + referral   78%
#     brief intervention + referral           37%
#     referral alone                          45%
#
# Chambers et al. (observational, in the 2025 systematic review PMC12912343)
# report aOR 5.86 (95% CI 2.70-12.71) for 30-day engagement after ED initiation.
#
# WHAT RHODE ISLAND ACTUALLY ACHIEVED IS FOUR TIMES LOWER. AnchorED has placed
# peer recovery specialists in RI EDs since 2014. Program reporting (Waye et al.,
# Addict Behav 2019; NASHP profile) gives referral to treatment at discharge
# rising from 9% to ~21%, with >85% of overdose cases involving a peer and 86.8%
# of patients agreeing to post-discharge outreach.
#
# 86.8% is WILLINGNESS, not linkage. The linkage number is ~21%.
#
# The ratio agrees with the trial (21/9 = 2.33 against D'Onofrio's 2.11); the
# LEVEL differs about fourfold, because AnchorED is peer navigation while
# D'Onofrio started buprenorphine in the ED. These are different interventions
# and should be different arms, not averaged.
#
# See docs/calibration_log/phase_7_intervention_evidence_2026-08-17.md section 2.1.
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FILL IN — Jun: pick ONE arm, or run both.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Each arm is `post_overdose_rr = <target linkage> / <fitted moud.reinit_prob>`.
#
# (a1) SCALE PEER NAVIGATION — what RI has actually done, extended statewide.
#      Target linkage 0.21 (AnchorED post-implementation referral rate).
#      Worked at trial 561's reinit_prob 0.11833:  0.21 / 0.11833 = 1.77
#      NOTE: part of this is already in the calibrated baseline, since AnchorED
#      has run since 2014 and the scored window is 2012-2022. Treat this arm as
#      "the remaining scale-up", and check what the baseline already encodes
#      before claiming the full 9% -> 21% as the contrast.
#
# (a2) ED-INITIATED BUPRENORPHINE — a clinical intervention RI has NOT deployed
#      at scale, and the one with RCT support. Target linkage 0.78 (D'Onofrio).
#      Worked at trial 561:  0.78 / 0.11833 = 6.59
#      This is the recommended primary result: it is a real policy choice, it has
#      the strongest evidence, and it is distinguishable from the baseline.
#
# (b) CEILING / UPPER BOUND (label it as such in the paper)
#     Saturate p_start to 1.0, i.e. every survivor linked within one step:
#
#         post_overdose_rr = 20.0     # the parameter's declared max
#
#     This clamps only if fitted reinit_prob >= 0.05 (since 0.05 x 20 = 1.0).
#     CHECK THAT AFTER THE REFIT. If reinit_prob lands below 0.05, arm (b) is
#     not reachable through this knob and would need the engine change that this
#     template previously proposed.
#
# ============================================================================
# moud:
#   post_overdose_rr: <FILL IN — see (a) or (b) above>
